From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:08:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Tidy and link previews answer through the AI that
 answers Ask
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tidy said "Add your Claude API key in Settings > AI to tidy tabs." to
someone with Claude Code signed in, and link previews never showed for
them: both went straight to Anthropic's API on a key. Now they ask whoever
answers Ask (CurrentProvider(): Claude Code, Codex incl. the VS Code
extension's, Gemini, Copilot, OpenCode, a local model, a cloud key, or
Claude on the Anthropic key), with the AI account of the tab's space, after
the same consent question. One path does it, AiService::Complete: Claude's
API keeps the JSON schema for Tidy; an agent or a model is asked for the
JSON in words and the answer is checked (ParseTidyPlan now also finds the
object in a code fence or between words).

With nothing to answer, every AI feature says the same thing: sign in to
the agent that is installed, or "Install Claude Code or connect an AI in
Settings › AI." Never "add an API key" alone. Settings, Tidy and the Chat
view stop saying Claude where it is whichever AI answers. Onboarding's
suggestions and Settings' "Check" run with the active space's account, as
Ask does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
